seful for turning information into clear visual structure."}, {"id": "0284b30f-e8ea-4edd-9491-890b20f20a32", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modular visual systems", "children": [{"id": "87ea32e1-86f5-40ae-b652-32c1f1b7ca2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Rules, modules, components, grids, symbols, variables, and repeatable templates"}, {"id": "83f11649-eea3-4dc9-99dc-702a398d8da9", "type": "concept", "title": "Series development for campaigns, packaging families, icon sets, and editorial systems"}, {"id": "5a9a75f6-8842-436b-9ba7-306bd1e41a8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation so another designer can extend the system"}], "description": "Students learn to create asset families that can expand without losing coherence."}]}, {"id": "b4226c3f-b0b2-4236-9c96-fe41f0a1ed81", "type": "topic", "title": "Cross-App Workflow, Libraries, Links, and Collaborative Production", "description": "Move vector assets cleanly among Photoshop, InDesign, Figma, motion, web, and production environments.", "children": [{"id": "02979b22-b62f-4f06-8530-28f71af06ca1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creative Cloud and asset workflow", "children": [{"id": "2f013f43-7aea-4294-ba5c-d6e94a2f1891", "type": "concept", "title": "Libraries, linked assets, embedded assets, package habits, cloud documents, and shared review"}, {"id": "1c475c2d-f7a6-4283-bcfe-6dde59febdf1", "type": "concept", "title": "Moving art into Photoshop, InDesign, After Effects, Figma, Acrobat, and web workflows"}, {"id": "8cf1f6e9-cafb-40fd-82e9-616c4932ef2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding missing links, broken fonts, profile changes, and unsupported effects"}], "description": "Illustrator files often sit inside larger design pipelines."}, {"id": "d335a6cb-087f-488e-bf35-8bdf5b86b051", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layer and asset organization", "children": [{"id": "faa6834b-b578-4830-a385-2536b8e85b2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Layer naming, groups, symbols, styles, swatches, templates, nonprinting layers, and